
  Check the OVDB.md and the manifests of a Git repository, as committed at HEAD, against the OVDB Directory's rules and
  the extra rules a publisher's own check holds a repository to.

  It reads the commit with git, never the working tree, so what you changed but did not commit is not checked. It needs
  git 2.45 or newer, and it never uses the network: nothing is fetched, nothing is sent.

  Exit codes: 0 no problems; 1 the repository is refused (the findings say why); 2 the command could not run as asked (a
  wrong flag or path, or git is missing or too old).

  The Directory also reads your hosted repository, so a pass here is not the Directory's acceptance.

  USAGE

    ovdb publisher check [path] [--flags]

  FLAGS

    -h --help     Help for check
    --json        Print the result as a JSON document for a CI job
    --repository  The repository this one is, as the manifests must say in publisher.repository (https://github.com/<owner>/<repository>)
